@* Everything in this folder stays on static server-side rendering.

   Sign-in writes an authentication cookie, which means writing a response header,
   which is impossible once an interactive circuit has taken over the response. The
   trap is that it appears to work: HttpContext is non-null during prerendering, so
   SignInAsync succeeds on the first render and silently stops working once the
   circuit connects.

   Excluding the whole area from interactive routing removes the possibility rather
   than relying on nobody adding @rendermode to a page here later. *@
@attribute [ExcludeFromInteractiveRouting]
